# Phase 3 & 4 Walkthrough: IPPO & MAPPO (CTDE) Baselines

This document summarizes the implementations, unit tests, training logs, and rigorous comparative evaluations for Phase 3 (Independent PPO) and Phase 4 (Multi-Agent PPO with CTDE) on SAGE-Traffic.

---

## 1. Phase 4 Architecture: Centralized Training with Decentralized Execution (CTDE)

1. **Centralized Critic ($V(S_t)$)** ([`models/mappo_network.py`](file:///c:/Users/kashi/OneDrive/Desktop/major/models/mappo_network.py)):
   - Conditioned strictly on the 172-dimensional concatenated global state $S_t = [o_A, o_B, o_C, o_D]$ ($4 \times 43$).
   - Architecture: $\text{Linear}(172, 128) \to \text{Tanh} \to \text{Linear}(128, 64) \to \text{Tanh} \to \text{Linear}(64, 1)$.
   - Consumes global state directly with no agent ID appended to the critic.
   - Evaluates the global scalar state-value estimate $V(S_t)$.

2. **Decentralized Actor(s)** ([`models/mappo_network.py`](file:///c:/Users/kashi/OneDrive/Desktop/major/models/mappo_network.py)):
   - **Decentralization Guarantee**: At execution time, actors receive ONLY their own local 43-dimensional observation.
   - **Shared Policy Mode (`share_policy: true`)**: Input dimension = 47 ($43 \text{ local obs} + 4\text{-dim one-hot agent ID}$). Output = 4 action logits.
   - **Individual Policy Mode (`share_policy: false`)**: Four separate actor networks ($43 \to 64 \to 64 \to 4$).

3. **GAE & Advantage Formulation**:
   - Evaluates team reward $r_{\text{global}, t} = \sum_{a \in \{A,B,C,D\}} r_{a,t}$.
   - TD error: $\delta_t = r_{\text{global}, t} + \gamma V(S_{t+1})(1 - d_t) - V(S_t)$.
   - Advantage: $A_t = \delta_t + \gamma \lambda (1 - d_t) A_{t+1}$. Target returns: $R_t = A_t + V(S_t)$.
   - Actors optimize clipped surrogate objective with normalized centralized advantage $\hat{A}_t$.

