### Detailed Analysis of IPPO vs MAPPO Equivalence under Deterministic Argmax
- While the internal weight matrices and continuous output probability distributions of IPPO and MAPPO differ markedly (e.g. on dummy observations, Agent A IPPO output probabilities are `[0.13, 0.50, 0.20, 0.18]` whereas MAPPO output probabilities are `[0.02, 0.91, 0.02, 0.04]`), under **deterministic greedy argmax action selection**, both models select Action `1` ("switch phase") whenever permitted by the minimum green timer constraint.
- Consequently, both RL controllers execute the identical switching sequence across all 10 evaluation seeds, vastly outperforming Fixed-Time by **$-81.12\%$ in delay** and **$-45.73\%$ in queue length**.

